      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5fca5df4d58780532024a52b|full_name}: Fair enough. I just hate to think of someone having to experience it in order for it to be reported in the first place. One instance of it happening sucks. Being directly targeted because you're sensitive to something is a pretty big risk to expose to anyone.\n\nI do agree with the sentiment, and it's possible this could work well if done 'correctly', but it's hard to say what the 'correct' solution here is though. Tough thing to balance imo.\n\nIt's essentially like putting a big \"Kick me! And this is where you can kick me so it hurts the most!\" sign on people's backs and would personally make me feel /more/ unsafe joining random worlds, even if it is moderated in theory.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
