      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 3
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Throwing my support behind this request as well. Having the ability to handle and respect users' content preferences without outright blocking them from experiencing worlds together with people would be great, especially when it's often just small elements or features in a world. It also empowers and encourages creators who might uncertain of the boundaries to be more generous in keeping within them.\n\nAs far as concerns of targeted abuse go, I don't expect that to be very common, and for the few that might they can be handled by the report system the same way as untagged worlds would be. After all, we have quest/pc differentiation exposed to udon, as well as vr/desktop, and on the whole the features are used for good to enhance the player experience.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
